From adcbeece73627ff72f29bfc59ea998cd12262203 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "@dev/6" <dev-6@main.hh.invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:38:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent-acp): list each record's own folder, so a
 same-account thread is not credited to another record

Codex records on one account share one CODEX_HOME, and session/list was
asked about no folder, so every record listed every thread of the account.
The host gives an unrecorded id to the first lister in load order, so a
native thread made in one seat's folder was credited to another seat's
record and `hab up --resume` was refused there (#38033).

- listedBy passes the record's cwd as ACP's session/list cwd filter, merged
  with the cursor, when the record names an absolute folder and the server
  runs on this host. No cwd, a relative cwd, or a machine listing asks about
  no folder, as before.
- find honours the host's recorded folder (SessionAt.workingDirectory): a
  session recorded outside the record's folder is in no filtered listing, so
  the catalogue's recorded-folder lookup now lists that folder on the
  record's listing server. Without this, the listing fix alone drops a
  recorded worktree session from the catalogue.
- Test: two same-account records in different folders, the wrong one loaded
  first; each thread goes to the record whose folder it ran in, and a
  recorded session in a third folder still lists under its recorded agent.
  The fixture takes ACP_LISTED as one shared store.
- The catalog test that pinned "lists every session whatever folder" now
  pins the filter for an absolute cwd and the old answer for none/relative.

Refs: @i/32986-agent-host/38033
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
